<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jonker Afrikaner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1790–<a href="/years/1861">1861</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jonker <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaner</a> was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oorlam">Oorlam</a> Afrikaners, a horse-riding, gun-using community from the Cape frontier. Around 1823 he moved north into central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> at the invitation of the Nama to fight the Herero, and by about 1840 settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windhoek">Windhoek</a>. His raiding and trading state dominated central Namibia until his death in 1861.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jonker-afrikaner.jpg" alt="Jonker Afrikaner" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles John Andersson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Ngami-p232.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>From the late 18th century Oorlam communities moved north from the Cape into Namaqualand, partly to escape conscription, and under <b>Jonker Afrikaner</b> came to dominate the Nama and fight the Herero.</blockquote><a href="/culture/khoekhoe">Khoekhoe · Contact &amp; Exchange</a></li><li><blockquote>The Herero, Bantu-speaking cattle herders of central Namibia, had been raided for decades by <b>Jonker Afrikaner's</b> Orlam Afrikaner State.</blockquote><a href="/state/herero-paramountcy">Herero Paramountcy</a></li><li><blockquote>Around 1823 his son <b>Jonker Afrikaner</b> moved north at the invitation of the Nama to help them against the Herero, and by about 1840 he had settled at Windhoek, which he made his capital.</blockquote><a href="/state/orlam-afrikaner-state">Orlam Afrikaner State</a></li></ul></section>
